('Level8_1','Level8_1_231','introvert','''ɪntrəvɝt','''ɪntrəvɜːt','[n] 内向','I sympathize with the introvert as I would with the sickly, but both are missing a lot of life.  我会像体谅体弱病残的人那样，体谅性格内向的人，但两者都失去许多人生体验。'),
('Level8_1','Level8_1_232','contemplation',',kɑntəm''pleʃən',',kɒntem''pleɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 沉思','The monks spend an hour in contemplation each morning.  那些修道士每天早上默想一小时。'),
('Level8_1','Level8_1_233','heed','hid','hiːd','[n&v] 注意；留心','If she had only heeded my warnings , none of this would have happened.  要是她当初听从我的警告，这一切都不会发生。'),
('Level8_1','Level8_1_234','cognition','kɑɡ''nɪʃən','kɒg''nɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 认知','the regions of the brain that are responsible for memory and cognition  大脑主管记忆与认知的区域'),
('Level8_1','Level8_1_235','suppression','sə''prɛʃən','sə''preʃ(ə)n','[n] 镇压；压制',''),
('Level8_1','Level8_1_236','inhibit','ɪn''hɪbɪt','ɪn''hɪbɪt','[v] 抑制','An unhappy family life may inhibit children’s learning.  不幸福的家庭生活可能会阻碍儿童的学习。'),
('Level8_1','Level8_1_237','obstruct','əb''strʌkt','əb''strʌkt','[v] 阻碍','A small aircraft was obstructing the runway.  一架小型飞机堵住了跑道。'),
