('SAT_3','SAT_3_1332','cataclysm','''kætəklɪzəm','''kætəklizəm','[n] 灾难； 大洪水；  大变动','In The Possessed the earth quakes: it is not the catastrophe that befalls the imaginative individual, but a cataclysm in which a large portion of humanity is buried, wiped out forever.  在《魔鬼》中发生了地震，这不仅是降临在富于想象力的人头上的大灾难，而是一大半人类被埋葬于其中、永远被消灭的大地震。'),
('SAT_3','SAT_3_1333','surreptitious',',sɝrəp''tɪʃəs','ˌsʌrəp''tiʃəs','[adj] 暗中的， 秘密的， 偷偷摸摸的','Rory tried to sneak a surreptitious glance at Adam’s wristwatch.  罗里试图偷偷看一眼亚当的手表。'),
('SAT_3','SAT_3_1334','transplant','træns''plænt','træns''plɑːnt','[v] 移植','The operation to transplant a kidney is now fairly routine.  移植肾脏的手术如今相当常见。'),
('SAT_3','SAT_3_1335','spineless','''spaɪnləs','''spainlis','[adj] 无脊椎的','A jellyfish is a spineless animal.  水母是无脊椎动物。'),
